//? Title: Levenshtein byte edit distance
//? Subtitle: Actual rolling rows, original kitten/sitting table and optimal edit paths
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Unit insertions, deletions and substitutions define the shortest edit path
between two byte strings. We retain the original examples and kitten/sitting
table, capture the rows actually produced by the two-row library kernel and
inspect an additional native optimal traceback. Byte semantics, optional capture
costs and the distinction from insertion/deletion-only LCS distance are
explicit.
)

\toc

> Prefix distances

Let D(i,j) compare prefixes of the actual row and column byte strings. Empty
boundaries cost their prefix lengths. Every edit path into an interior cell ends
with a deletion, insertion or diagonal match/substitution, giving

$$D(i,j)=\min\{D(i-1,j)+1,D(i,j-1)+1,D(i-1,j-1)+[r_{i-1}\ne c_{j-1}]\}.$$
\alttext(The actual edit table takes the least cost among deletion, insertion and a zero-cost match or unit-cost substitution.)

Induction over prefix lengths proves shortest-path optimality. The ordinary
implementation keeps only two rolling rows, placing the shorter input in
columns; equal lengths put original b in rows. Capture copies each genuinely
computed row after the producer swaps buffers. An additional native traceback
then reads that captured table, preferring an optimal diagonal, then up, then
left. This extra work is explicitly absent from the ordinary scalar call.

> A tiny actual substitution

Comparing a and b costs1, whereas insertion/deletion-only distance would cost2.
The concept diagram uses the real captured boundary alternatives and actual
selected diagonal path cost.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/levenshtein_substitution.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::levenshtein_trace("a", "b");
    auto e = t.path[0];
    std::print("| actual distance | actual diagonal cost | actual row prefix | actual column prefix | " "actual predecessor row | actual predecessor column |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               t.analysis.distance, e.cost, e.row, e.column, e.next_row,
               e.next_column);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("diagonal", {0, 2},
           std::format("Actual D(0,0)={}\nplus substitution1", t.table[0][0])).node("neighbors", {0, -2}, std::format("Actual upper/left\n{}, {} plus1", t.table[0][1], t.table[1][0])).node("cell", {7, 0}, std::format("Actual D(1,1)={}\nselected path cost{}", t.table[1][1], e.cost)).edge("diagonal", "cell").edge("neighbors", "cell").save_svg("build/levenshtein_substitution.svg");
}
```
